---
// FAQ Section with JSON-LD Schema for SEO Rich Snippets
const faqs = [
  {
    q: "What are the passing criteria to earn an Official Typing Certificate?",
    a: "To qualify for an Official Certificate of Typing Proficiency, a candidate must achieve a Net Speed strictly exceeding 20 Words Per Minute (>20 WPM, i.e., at least 21 WPM) for any Nepali layout (Unicode Traditional, Romanized, or Preeti ASCII), or strictly exceeding 25 Words Per Minute (>25 WPM, i.e., at least 26 WPM) for English US QWERTY. Additionally, a minimum typing accuracy of 85.0% is required."
  },
  {
    q: "How can employers or institutions verify my typing certificate?",
    a: "Every certificate issued by TopNepali Typing contains a unique alphanumeric identifier (e.g., TN-2026-X8K9M2), a secure verification QR code, and a tamper-evident cryptographic signature. Anyone can verify the authenticity of a certificate instantly by entering the ID into the public verification portal at typing.topnepali.com/verify or scanning the QR code."
  },
  {
    q: "What is the technical difference between Nepali Unicode and Preeti Font?",
    a: "Preeti is a legacy 8-bit ASCII font mapping created in the 1990s that replaces Latin glyphs with Devanagari shapes. Texts typed in Preeti cannot be searched on Google, indexed by search engines, or viewed properly on devices lacking the specific font file. Nepali Unicode (UTF-8) is the international ISO standard for Devanagari, ensuring that text is universally readable, searchable, and exchangeable across all computers, smartphones, and web services."
  },
  {
    q: "What is the United Nations General Assembly (UNGA) Speech Examination?",
    a: "The certification examination utilizes the historic address delivered by Mayor Balendra (Balen) Shah to the United Nations General Assembly on Himalayan climate crisis, mountain community resilience, and global climate justice. Candidates can take the test as a Complete Speech Challenge (typing until the conclusion of the speech) or choose standardized 5-minute or 10-minute timed benchmarks."
  },
  {
    q: "How does the AI-driven Adaptive Weak Key Drill algorithm work?",
    a: "Our adaptive engine tracks millisecond latency and error frequency for every physical key you strike. When it detects elevated hesitation or mistakes on specific keys (e.g., 'w' and 'o' in English, or 'ध' and '्' in Nepali), it queries a pre-indexed dictionary using a density scoring function. This surfaces words with high co-occurrence of your exact weak keys, accelerating muscle memory formation through targeted neural repetition."
  },
  {
    q: "Do I need to download or install any font packages to use this platform?",
    a: "No installation is required. TopNepali Typing automatically bundles and streams high-definition web fonts—including Kokila for standard Devanagari and authentic Preeti for legacy ASCII layouts—directly into your browser cache, enabling instant plug-and-play practice on any PC, Mac, Chromebook, or tablet."
  },
  {
    q: "How are Net WPM and Typing Consistency calculated?",
    a: "We implement international typing standards where 1 word equals exactly 5 keystrokes. Raw WPM measures total keystrokes divided by 5 per minute, while Net WPM strictly credits correct keystrokes. Consistency (%) measures the uniformity of your keystroke rhythm by calculating the coefficient of variation (CV) across your inter-keystroke intervals (IKIs)."
  }
];
---

<section class="mt-12 mb-16">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
    <div class="text-center mb-8">
      <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-[var(--accent-primary)] block mb-1">Got Questions?</span>
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold font-display text-[var(--text-primary)]">
        Frequently Asked Questions
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-4">
      {faqs.map((faq) => (
        <details class="bg-[var(--bg-surface)] border border-[var(--border-subtle)] rounded-2xl p-5 group transition-all duration-200 hover:border-[var(--border-focus)]/50">
          <summary class="font-bold text-sm text-[var(--text-primary)] cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between gap-4">
            <span>{faq.q}</span>
            <span class="text-xs text-[var(--text-muted)] group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform duration-200">▼</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-xs leading-relaxed text-[var(--text-secondary)] border-t border-[var(--border-subtle)] pt-3">
            {faq.a}
          </p>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- JSON-LD Structured Data for FAQPage -->
<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": faqs.map(f => ({
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": f.q,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": f.a
    }
  }))
})} />
